      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(cli): isolate desktop context service tests",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- keep desktop-context clipboard tests isolated from live macOS application and window services\n- use deterministic empty stubs when a test does not provide application/window fixtures\n- allow the application stub to represent an unavailable frontmost application\n\n## Why\n\nThe release preflight hung on macOS 27 inside `NSApplication` initialization because the clipboard-only tests accidentally fell back to Peekaboo's real window enumeration service. Unit tests should not touch the host desktop when their fixtures omit unrelated services.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `swift test --package-path Apps/CLI -Xswiftc -DPEEKABOO_SKIP_AUTOMATION --filter DesktopContextServiceClipboardGatingTests --no-parallel` (3 tests passed in 0.043 seconds)\n- `pnpm run format`\n- autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
